.TH FOUNDRY-CREATE-USB.SH 1 "2026-11-14" "Foundry Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
foundry-create-usb.sh \- download a Foundry ISO and prepare installation media
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B foundry-create-usb.sh
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads the selected Foundry Linux ISO, verifies its published SHA256 checksum,
and opens it in isoimagewriter or usb-creator-kde.
A local ISO may be selected instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--iso " PATH
Use a local ISO instead of downloading. Local images are not checksum-verified
by this script.
.TP
.BI "--device " DEV
Write directly to the named block device using dd. This erases the device.
The script rejects mounted partitions and undersized devices, then asks for
the exact confirmation YES. Writing requires appropriate device permissions.
.TP
.BI "--edition " NAME
Select the edition to download; the default is anvil.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B EDITION
sets the default edition; --edition overrides it.
.SH FILES
Downloaded images are cached in ~/Downloads/.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dd (1),
.BR sha256sum (1)
